<article class="env-lemma" id="0CVH">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CVH">Lemma <span data-tag="0CVH">77.3.5</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0CV6" data-tag="0CV6">77.2.1</a>. Let $i : Z \to X$ be a closed immersion and assume that $\mathcal{F} = i_*\mathcal{G}$ for some finite type, quasi-coherent sheaf $\mathcal{G}$ on $Z$. Then $\mathcal{G}$ is (universally) pure above $y$ if and only if $\mathcal{F}$ is (universally) pure above $y$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Divisors on Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/0CV4" data-tag="0CV4">71.4.9</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>